In tonight's programme we begin in the east of the Democratic Republic of Congo, where children have died after a school fire broke out in the M23 rebel occupied city of Bukavu. Also, Senegal looks to the skies as it seeks to develop its home-grown satellite industry. And finally, we wonder about the future of African cities. How will they cope with the population boom and climate crisis? A question, the Kenya architecture biennale in Nairobi tried to answer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e54c4920-ae1d-11f1-ae7e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10961424326aa461fc83f3e6-90411594.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e54c4920-ae1d-11f1-ae7e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10961424326aa461fc83f3e6-90411594.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96972eb8-ae1c-11f1-88ff-eb2137a3fed2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:18:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clémence WALLER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran-backed Houthis seize near control of vital Bab el-Mandeb shipping lane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane</link><description>
Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels captured the strategic Perim Island in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, located at the southern entrance to the Red Sea, officials said on Friday. The lightning move opens a new front in the Iran war and threatens energy supplies, especially Saudi oil exports, from passing through one of the world's key shipping lanes. 
