Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged US President Donald Trump to impose new sanctions on Russia over deadly strikes on Ukraine, as Kyiv and Moscow step up attacks and US-led efforts to end the war remain deadlocked. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aaae0618-ae0f-11f1-9530-115fa1eedc7a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:13:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg">© Leonhard Foeger, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Can we slowdown AI, and 9/11, who has the right to remember?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember</link><description>
